# The port's half of the neutron check; its partner is neutron_nogeneral.mac.
#
# MEASURED, 2,000 events of 100 MeV:
#
#   neutron   port 0 pGy exactly   Geant4 0 pGy exactly
#
# Both zero, and the zero is the point: a neutron with no cross section is a
# G4Transportation-only track, so it crosses the world in straight lines and leaves with its
# energy. The same Geant4 run with NeutronGeneralProc ACTIVE is what the neutron's hadronic
# physics is worth for this geometry, and that number belongs to P8.
#
# A dose of zero cannot tell "streamed out" from "never stepped", so the streaming itself is
# asserted in tests/test_neutron.cu instead: one step of 200 mm + the navigator's push, a clock
# advanced by L/(beta c) to 1.5589200855 ns, energy unchanged, edep exactly zero, and the track
# leaving the world. That test also covers the 10 us time cut, which no shower here can reach.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/gun/particle neutron
/gun/energy 100 MeV

/run/printProgress 500
/run/beamOn 2000
